    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ālĭus</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ālĕus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj., = Elius (v. Alis and Elis),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Elian;
			subst.</i>, <i>a native of Elis</i>, <i>a town in Achaia</i> (only a few times in Plaut. Capt.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postquam belligerant Aetoli cum Aleis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. prol. 24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 2, 30</span></i>.</div>
